# Copy to .env beside this file before `docker compose up`.

# REQUIRED. The public domain, resolving to this host's edge.
# Chosen once: every account address embeds it, and changing the server
# means creating new accounts. No scheme, no port, just the name.
ENCLAVE_DOMAIN=enclave.example.pt

# --- standalone mode: Caddy owns 80/443 and fetches TLS itself ------------
# ENCLAVE_SITE_ADDRESS defaults to ENCLAVE_DOMAIN; binds default to 80/443.
#ENCLAVE_SITE_ADDRESS=
#ENCLAVE_HTTP_BIND=80
#ENCLAVE_HTTPS_BIND=443

# --- behind-proxy mode: host nginx/traefik terminates TLS -----------------
# The container speaks plain HTTP on loopback; see infra/nginx-enclave.conf.
# The 443 bind is unused in this mode, parked on loopback to avoid clashing
# with the host proxy.
#ENCLAVE_SITE_ADDRESS=:80
#ENCLAVE_HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1:8080
#ENCLAVE_HTTPS_BIND=127.0.0.1:8443

# Days the server keeps ciphertext for offline members. 0 keeps nothing
# beyond live delivery. This is the operator's main privacy dial.
ENCLAVE_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# Comma-separated server names allowed to federate.
#
# EMPTY MEANS FEDERATION IS OFF, not open. This file said "open" and the code
# has meant the opposite since the day the check was tightened: an envelope's
# signature proves nothing about legitimacy here, because the verifying key is
# fetched from the very origin the envelope names. Left open, anyone with a
# domain could sign their own way in, be recorded as a peer of a channel, and
# receive every future message in it, including the account address carried in
# each welcome.
#
# Federation stays off until you name the peers you actually trust.
ENCLAVE_FEDERATION_ALLOWLIST=

# The room every account on this server joins. Empty switches the idea off.
# Anyone with an account here can ask to be let in, and a member's client
# answers automatically, so treat everything said in it as public. See the
# common room section of docs/THREAT-MODEL.md before switching it on.
#ENCLAVE_COMMON_ROOM=!orwell:enclave.example.pt

# Let every account on this server learn which other accounts exist here.
# Off by default and it should stay off on any server whose users do not
# already know each other: handing out the account list is a betrayal of the
# people on it. It exists for the familial deployment, where "who else is here"
# was never a secret.
#ENCLAVE_COMMUNITY_MODE=false

# The oldest app version this server lets in. Empty refuses nobody. When set,
# an older app (or one that does not send its version, like every app before
# 1.0) gets the error `versao-antiga` and a sentence asking the person to
# reload or download the new version.
#ENCLAVE_VERSAO_MINIMA_DO_CLIENTE=1.0.0

# --- SFU: the media relay for calls ---------------------------------------
#
# One port for call media, UDP and TCP on the same number. mediasoup's
# WebRtcServer multiplexes every transport through it.
#
# EMPTY OR MISSING MEANS ZERO, AND ZERO MEANS NO SFU. The server still starts,
# the gateway still answers, and clients make peer-to-peer calls instead.
# Turning it off later needs no migration.
#
# Open both protocols in the firewall, for example with UFW:
#   ufw allow 44300/udp
#   ufw allow 44300/tcp
#ENCLAVE_SFU_PORT=44300

# The public address the relay announces to clients (ICE candidates).
#
# REQUIRED when the SFU runs inside Docker. The worker only sees the bridge's
# internal address (172.x), and without this every client is told to connect to
# a machine it cannot reach. The call negotiates fine and never connects, and
# the logs say all went well.
#
# The host's public IP address, not the domain.
#ENCLAVE_SFU_ANNOUNCED_IP=203.0.113.7

# --- Outgoing bandwidth ----------------------------------------------------
#
# The relay's total outgoing budget across all calls, in Mbit/s. Empty uses
# the defaults (300 for video, 40 kept for voice). See
# apps/server/src/orcamento-de-saida.ts.
#ENCLAVE_ORCAMENTO_VIDEO_MBPS=300
#ENCLAVE_RESERVA_VOZ_MBPS=40

# Monthly traffic quota. infra/quota-vnstat.sh (run by cron on the host, see
# infra/quota-vnstat.cron) writes this month's outgoing bytes to a small JSON
# file that the container reads. From 80 % of the quota, new video admissions
# drop to the reduced budget. A missing or stale file (older than 2 hours) is
# ignored.
#ENCLAVE_QUOTA_MENSAL_TB=8
#ENCLAVE_ORCAMENTO_VIDEO_REDUZIDO_MBPS=50

# --- Reports ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Closed reports are kept this many days (longer while a suspension is
# running). The copy sent to the channel founder is delayed by a random number
# of hours in this range.
#ENCLAVE_DENUNCIAS_DIAS=90
#ENCLAVE_DENUNCIA_ATRASO_HORAS=1-6

# --- Site donation meter -----------------------------------------------------
#
# A GoFundMe campaign URL that the server reads every 15 minutes and serves at
# /_enclave/apoiar.json. Visitors never talk to GoFundMe. Set it to empty to
# switch the meter off.
#ENCLAVE_CAMPANHA_GOFUNDME=
